const BEFORE_STORY_OSAKA_CRY='I NEED TO GET TO A HOSPITAL! AHHHHH!';
const BEFORE_STORY_OSAKA_ENCOUNTER=[
 ['boki','Look at this, stranger. I have obtained the power to save my nephew Tajiri! I am awakened.'],
 ['josiah','Tajiri is still out there, Boki. We can find him. Tell me what you touched, and step away from it.'],
 ['boki','For years I called his name into empty rooms. Now the stones answer me. The thread has become a chain, and I can pull him home.'],
 ['josiah','A chain can drag someone under just as easily as it can bring them back. You do not know what this power will ask of you.'],
 ['boki','I know what grief has already taken. Takeshi. Bozuki. A child with nobody left to shelter him. I will not let Tajiri become another empty chair.'],
 ['josiah','Then let me help you protect him. You do not have to become something he would be frightened to come home to.'],
 ['boki','You speak as though sorrow can be filed away in one of your reports. I have crossed the dark between prayers, stranger. I will not go back with empty hands.'],
 ['josiah','I am not here to write a report. I am asking you to stop before someone gets hurt. Look at me, Boki. You still have a choice.'],
 ['boki','Then look closely, stranger. I am the Antichrist. This is what the castle has placed in my hands. No government, no frightened little man will keep me from Tajiri.'],
 ['josiah','The Antichrist? Boki, put it down. Whatever you think it has promised you—do not fire that at me!']
];
const BEFORE_STORY_OSAKA_RECOVERY=[
 ['josiah','The glitching has stopped. For two days, every time I closed my eyes, the castle returned in broken pieces: the stone, the light in her hands, the moment my own body ceased to obey me. Now the walls remain where they belong. My hands are steady. I should be relieved.'],
 ['josiah','They tell me I was found outside Osaka Castle. I remember the steps scraping beneath my palms, and I remember trying to shout for a hospital. Everything after that is a corridor with the lights switched off. Someone carried me through it, but no one here can tell me who.'],
 ['josiah','Boki spoke of saving Tajiri as though the world had already agreed to her terms. I had gone looking for answers about a family, a fortress, and a power that could bind nations. I left with a wound the doctors cannot explain and a question I can no longer afford to dismiss.'],
 ['josiah','The priest told me I would help him reach the stars, whether I liked it or not. I have spent years treating those words as the last confusion of a dying man. After what happened in that room, they sound less like a confession and more like an appointment someone made on my behalf.'],
 ['josiah','I want to believe this is recovery. That the silence means it is over, that whatever passed from her hands into me has finally burnt itself out. Yet there is a coldness beside the bed, where the sunlight should be warm. The glitching has stopped. Something else has begun.'],
 ['figure','From India to Hong Kong, Britannia rules the waves.'],
 ['josiah','What? India… Hong Kong? Who are you? What does that have to do with me? I was in Osaka. How did you get into this room?'],
 ["crown","You may call me Union Crown. Do not look at the door; I did not need to open it. You have been waiting for me since the castle, though you keep calling that waiting an illness. It is a cruel thing, Josiah, to mistake your own awakening for damage."],
 ["crown","Boki did not break you. She stripped away the little protections that kept you ordinary. The doctors see a wound because wounds are all they know how to name. You felt something greater, and now you are allowing strangers to persuade you that your own senses cannot be trusted."],
 ["crown","You remember crawling, but memory is a frightened servant. It rearranges the furniture until its master believes the room was always small. You were not crawling away from power. You were carrying it out of the castle, exactly as you were meant to do."],
 ["crown","Only you can unite the world under this power. Not Boki, who would spend eternity searching for one child. Not your ministers, who mistake signatures for strength. You alone possess the patience to turn a thousand competing voices into one enduring command."],
 ["crown","Think of the lives lost while governments congratulate themselves on restraint. Every border becomes another excuse to abandon someone beyond it. When you refuse the power to end that suffering, is it really humility? Or is it simply cowardice wearing the respectable face of a civil servant?"],
 ["crown","The priest recognised you. You pretend his words were confusion because admitting he was right would make your responsibility unavoidable. He did not threaten you when he spoke of the stars. He offered you a future, and you have been hiding from it ever since."],
 ["crown","You need not ask the world for permission to save it. A frightened child struggles against the hand that pulls him from a fire. That struggle does not make the rescuer a tyrant. When nations resist you, remember that their resistance is proof of how desperately they need your guidance."],
 ["crown","They will call your chains oppression because they cannot bear to admit how comfortably they have lived inside weaker ones. Give them peace that cannot be overturned, order that cannot be negotiated away. In time, even those who curse your name will thank you for making obedience simple."],
 ["crown","Listen to your heart. That quickening is not fear; it is recognition. The room is not closing around you. Your old life is becoming too small to contain what you are. Anyone who tells you otherwise would rather keep you helpless than watch you become necessary."],
 ["crown","From India to Hong Kong, and beyond every coast their maps dared to name, one crown could gather the scattered world. Only you can make that unity permanent, Josiah. I will leave you now. When the silence returns, do not mistake it for freedom. It is merely the space where your answer belongs."],
 ["josiah","No—wait! Where did you go? I cannot… I cannot get enough air. My heart—something is wrong. This is fear. You do not get to tell me it is not fear! Somebody, please! I need someone in here! I cannot make it stop!"]
];
